From 87a49341341c0f7f16454c24f49fa2a795c7a316 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:53:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(protocol): update Bedrock to 1.26.60

Target the released protocol 2225 rather than advertise the old 2193
packet layouts under a new version name. Decode the added actor seat,
animation hand, chunk biome, dimension cloud and editor migration fields;
move PlayFab identity from skin data to player-list entries and encode the
new interaction and release hand fields.

Regenerate protocol enums, resource packs, particles, sounds, palette and
item IDs from the 1.26.60 metadata and matching 1.26.60.5 client. Map native
redstone connection states directly and normalize legacy connected blocks
without erasing explicit values at the unchanged state version. Supply
Java type and shape fallbacks for experimental content without claiming
complete feature parity. Signed audio and block seating remain unsupported
Java features and are canceled explicitly.

Sources: Mojang/bedrock-protocol-docs release v1.26.60 (protocol 2225),
GeyserMC/Geyser a24ba9c8f07b38be6455e5e86d187a2ef2ffa6a8, and the
bubbles-wow/mcbe-gdk-unpack-archive 1.26.60.5 release. Record asset hashes
and the stable-versus-experimental entity evidence in Data Asset Sources.

Validate the standalone patch on the pinned upstream base with build,
style checks, packet-boundary tests and mapping validation. An isolated
official BDS 1.26.60.6 bootstrap reaches StartGame and captures its actor
registry with the unchanged production login helper.

Keep the uint16 NetworkSettings no-compression sentinel separate from the
uint8 frame-header sentinel. Both are all-ones at their respective width;
after the enum update, decoding an uncompressed frame must still admit
0xFF. Cover the negotiated codec boundary in a buffer-level regression.

Consume and retain the uncompressed frame payload as a slice so decoder
progress does not depend on the next handler advancing its buffer.
